WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:07.410
There's an art to finding the right actor
for a role, and sometimes, filmmakers need

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.240
to see what they don't want before they're
able to settle on what they do.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.519
It's easy to imagine that the stars who play
our favorite film characters were the first

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:18.000
and only people considered, but that's not
always the case.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.779
Hard as it might be to believe, these iconic
roles could easily have ended up in different

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:22.869
hands.

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:25.500
Stuart Townsend as Aragorn

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.779
Everyone is familiar with Viggo Mortensen's
captivating portrayal of Aragorn, the Ranger

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:33.120
of the North and eventual King of Gondor in
The Lord of the Rings.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.750
As great as he is, Mortensen actually scooped
the role from Stuart Townsend, who spent two

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.040
months training before he was let go.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.360
Townsend would go on to his own successes,
but he didn't look back on his brush with

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.200
Middle-earth fondly, telling Entertainment
Weekly,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.530
"I did get shafted.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.500
I was there rehearsing and training for two
months, then was fired the day before filming

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.500
began."

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.330
That’s some Sauron-level treachery right
there.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.140
Sean Connery as Gandalf

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.760
Yes, Peter Jackson and his team originally
intended for crotchety Sean Connery to play

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.850
Gandalf the Grey, but Connery refused.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.050
It’s not the first big role Connery turned
down, either.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.780
Other rejected roles include Dumbledore from
the Harry Potter series, John Hammond from

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:12.580
Jurassic Park, and Morpheus in The Matrix.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.710
As far as The Lord of the Rings casting went,
he told The New Zealand Herald,

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.150
"I never understood it.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:18.150
I read the book.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.150
I read the script.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.150
I saw the movie.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:21.150
I still don't understand it.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.409
I would be interested in doing something that
I didn't fully understand, but not for 18

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:25.409
months."

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:28.920
Luckily, we ended up with Sir Ian McKellen
as the lovable wizard instead.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.020
Will Smith as Django

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.250
The list of R-rated movies starring Will Smith
is pretty short, but despite this, he was

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.210
originally written in as the hero in Django
Unchained.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.390
He didn't pass on the movie just to maintain
his wholesome image, however.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.370
Smith revealed to Entertainment Weekly that
he didn’t want to play the character after

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.830
finding out that he wasn’t originally going
to be playing the lead, or going to be killing

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.140
the bad guy.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:53.100
After the Fresh Prince passed, Django became
the lead character anyway, with Christoph

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:57.620
Waltz's Dr. King Schultz stepping aside for
Jamie Foxx to take the spotlight.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:58.890
Sorry, Will.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.690
Robert Downey Jr. as Lt. Matthew Kowalski

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:05.220
When we think about Robert Downey, Jr. these
days, we tend to picture his head stuck in

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.220
the Iron Man helmet.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.670
But picture Tony Stark as Sandra Bullock's
co-star in Gravity.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.019
As he told Howard Stern, Downey passed on
the role because he just couldn’t stand

00:02:13.019 --> 00:02:15.599
the special effects rig that he was strapped
into.

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:19.540
Coincidentally, Scarlett Johansson was also
a potential candidate for Bullock's role.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:23.329
We're pretty sure two Avengers could've made
it back from space with no problems.

00:02:23.329 --> 00:02:27.989
But then again, there’s only so many times
we can see Downey floating helplessly in space.

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:29.519
Chris Farley as Shrek

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:33.510
Mike Myers' performance as the lovable ogre
helped make Shrek an instant classic.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.739
But prior to Myers voicing the green guy,
a large portion of the film's dialogue was

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:38.219
recorded by Chris Farley.

00:02:38.219 --> 00:02:39.219
“Bah!

00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:40.219
Help!

00:02:40.219 --> 00:02:43.790
A big, stupid, stinky, smelly, ugly ogre.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:47.180
I’m so scared!”

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.500
His untimely death in 1997 derailed production,
resulting in major delays.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.129
Luckily, Shrek was able to find a suitable
voice courtesy of Farley's friend and former

00:02:55.129 --> 00:02:57.569
Saturday Night Live castmate.

00:02:57.569 --> 00:03:01.629
Meg Ryan, Diane Lane, and Michelle Pfeiffer
as Vivian Ward

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:05.769
Pretty Woman pretty much launched Julia Roberts'
career, but she only got the role of the hooker

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:09.489
with a heart of gold after a bunch of bigger
names passed first.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:13.719
Director Garry Marshall originally had Meg
Ryan lined up to play the part of Vivian Ward.

00:03:13.719 --> 00:03:17.439
After she departed the project, Diane Lane
got as far as costume fittings before dropping

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:18.439
out.

00:03:18.439 --> 00:03:21.920
Michelle Pfeiffer caught Marshall's eye, but
she also declined the role, leaving it in

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.460
the hands of the relatively unknown Roberts,
who was just 21 at the time.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.829
It turned out that she was the perfect person
to fall in love with Richard Gere on-screen,

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:31.749
and sell a truckload of Roxette records along
the way.

00:03:31.749 --> 00:03:33.760
Meryl Streep as Ellen Ripley

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.159
Sigourney Weaver broke cinematic barriers
of female badassery in the Alien franchise,

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:41.109
but the production team originally had its
eye on Meryl Streep for the role of Ellen

00:03:41.109 --> 00:03:42.230
Ripley.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.719
The actress dropped out prior to the start
of production because of the death of her

00:03:45.719 --> 00:03:47.930
boyfriend, Godfather actor John Cazale.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.900
Upon Streep's exit, Scott briefly turned to
Veronica Cartwright to play Ripley, and then

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:54.359
switched things up again, giving the role
to Weaver.

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:57.299
Cartwright was instead given the part of Chief
Navigator Lambert.

00:03:57.299 --> 00:04:01.480
Several decades and classic films later, it's
obvious he made the right choice.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:02.480
O.J.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.480
Simpson as The Terminator

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.709
Surprisingly, Arnold Schwarzenegger had to
juke past a football great to score the role

00:04:07.709 --> 00:04:12.219
of the unrelenting T-800 cyborg in the 1984
sci-fi classic The Terminator.

00:04:12.219 --> 00:04:15.989
Entertainment Weekly reported that Orion Pictures
co-founder Mike Medavoy wanted O.J.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.700
Simpson to star as the Terminator, saying,

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:18.870
"At the time, O.J.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:22.199
Simpson had one of those commercials for Hertz
where he jumped over a counter and ran to

00:04:22.199 --> 00:04:23.199
get a rental car.

00:04:23.199 --> 00:04:26.500
It was all of that athletic stuff, which I
thought the Terminator should have.”

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:30.870
Medavoy was so set on having Simpson as the
T-800 that he offered Schwarzenegger the role

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.460
of Kyle Reese, which would ultimately be played
by Michael Biehn.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.620
Thankfully, common sense intervened.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.470
Or maybe it was Skynet.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.620
Bill Murray as Batman

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.379
By the time Michael Keaton donned the Caped
Crusader's cowl, another take on the character

00:04:44.379 --> 00:04:46.610
had already spent years in development.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:50.740
An earlier project simply called The Batman
had stalled due to the deaths of a few potential

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:54.250
casting choices, and director Ivan Reitman
took the reigns.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.099
In his new version, he initially wanted Bill
Murray to play Batman, with Eddie Murphy as

00:04:58.099 --> 00:04:59.099
Robin.

00:04:59.099 --> 00:05:01.539
When you think about Keaton's Bruce Wayne,
the idea of Bill Murray in the part doesn't

00:05:01.539 --> 00:05:05.539
seem all that far-fetched… except maybe
picturing him in the Batsuit.

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:09.389
Eventually, Warner Bros. handed the reins
to Tim Burton, who axed The Batman's script

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:13.240
completely and gave us the 1989 Batman we
all know and love.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.389
Everyone in Ghostbusters

00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:19.020
Believe it or not, Paul "Pee-Wee Herman" Reubens
was originally intended to play Gozer the

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.330
Gozerian at the end of Ghostbusters.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.900
That's just one of the many ways in which
the 1984 comedy-horror classic changed during

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.349
its journey to the screen.

00:05:26.349 --> 00:05:30.449
Dan Aykroyd, who wrote the script with Meatballs
and Animal House vet Harold Ramis, originally

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:34.360
envisioned a futuristic time-traveling adventure
starring himself and fellow Blues Brother

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.919
and SNL pal John Belushi.

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:40.280
Understanding that the original concept would
have made Ghostbusters too expensive to film,

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:45.139
Ramis helped reshape the story, but Belushi's
untimely death in 1982 threw a wrench into

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:46.139
development.

00:05:46.139 --> 00:05:49.530
The movie was eventually rewritten into the
ensemble story we know and love, with Belushi

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.110
there in spirit, too.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.940
According to director Ivan Reitman, the glowing
green ghost known as Slimer was conceived

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:56.250
as a tribute to Belushi.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.879
It’s not hard to tell how.

00:05:57.879 --> 00:06:02.060
Ramis and Aykroyd also wanted John Candy to
star as Louis Tully, but Candy passed on the

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:03.060
project.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.250
The role eventually went to Rick Moranis.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:09.080
To top things off, before Ernie Hudson joined
the cast as Winston Zeddemore, Aykroyd originally

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.699
wanted his Trading Places co-star Eddie Murphy
for the role.

00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:15.009
Murphy had to pass because he was shooting
Beverly Hills Cop, but that's alright, because

00:06:15.009 --> 00:06:17.490
Ernie Hudson loves this town.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.460
“I love this town!”

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.729
Just About Everyone as Sam Wheat

00:06:22.729 --> 00:06:26.430
Despite the wishes of Ghost writer Bruce Joel
Rubin, who wanted the role of Sam Wheat to

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:30.740
go to Patrick Swayze, director Jerry Zucker
went through a slew of noteworthy actors to

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.729
star as the film’s dead lothario.

00:06:32.729 --> 00:06:36.850
According to IMDb, some of the names who turned
down the film's title role include Johnny

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:43.099
Depp, Kevin Bacon, Nicolas Cage, Kevin Costner,
Tom Cruise, Harrison Ford, Mel Gibson, Tom

00:06:43.099 --> 00:06:45.570
Hanks, John Travolta, and Alec Baldwin.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:49.699
Even Bruce Willis, who was married to Ghost
star Demi Moore at the time, passed on the

00:06:49.699 --> 00:06:50.699
project.

00:06:50.699 --> 00:06:53.289
Eventually Zucker came around to Rubin's way
of thinking, which was definitely for the

00:06:53.289 --> 00:06:54.289
best.

00:06:54.289 --> 00:06:57.360
We really couldn't imagine any more supernatural
scenes with Nic Cage.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:58.669
“I’m a vampire!

00:06:58.669 --> 00:06:59.990
I’m a vampire!

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:01.300
I’m a vampire!

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.620
I’m a vampire!

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:03.930
I’m a vampire!

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:05.249
I’m a vampire!”

00:07:05.249 --> 00:07:06.580
Thanks for watching!

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:09.389
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:07:09.389 --> 00:07:12.620
And leave us a comment to let us know which
alternate actors you would like to have seen

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.159
in these roles...

